<title>CANADA: Canada Oct department store sales rise on month.</title>
<headline>Canada Oct department store sales rise on month.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian department stores sales rose a seasonally adjusted 0.4 percent in October from September to C$1.22 billion, Statistics Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>In unadjusted data, year-over-year sales in October rose 7.7 percent to C$1.27 billion.</p>
<p>Sales at major stores rose 3.9 percent to C$557.6 million in October from the same month a year earlier. Consumer spending in the discount stores rose 11.0 percent to C$709.8 million from the same month a year earlier.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Mary Beth Garneau, Retail Trade Section, Industry Division, 613-951-9824.)</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745</p>
